/-- Complete reachable radius-three data, losslessly factored by repeated
weight triples. The low 19 bits encode the mask; the quotient modulo 6
encodes the ordering; its quotient by 6 selects a weight triple.
The expanded rows are (mask, all-order lower, chosen upper, SRL lower, order).
The companion theorems check these actual expanded data against geometry. -/
def radiusThreeRows : List (ℕ × ℕ × ℕ × ℕ × ℕ) :=
  packedRows.map fun code =>
    let weights := weightClasses[code / 524288 / 6]!
    (code % 524288, weights.1, weights.2.1, weights.2.2, code / 524288 % 6)

end D5.S3.StatisticalMechanics.HardCore.RadiusThreeData
